  "model": "s2.1-pro-free",
  "text": "These loaves are for people who ordered them earlier. They’re counting on me. I’ve moved the flour out of the puddle, but I can’t spend the day chasing sacks across the floor. I need to start baking.\n\nThe flour is dry! Sol’s repair means I can keep my promise. First we’ll mix the dough. Then we’ll divide and shape it into similar-sized loaves so they bake evenly.\n\nThat lump was too large to bake evenly. We still have dry flour for a new batch. This time, we can divide and shape the dough before it goes into the oven.\n\nThere’s the bread I promised. I’d like Sol to have one loaf as a thank-you. He thinks fixing a tile was only a little job, but it made all this possible.\n\nThe dough is ready to shape. Similar-sized loaves will bake evenly. A single large lump would take longer in the middle than our recipe allows.\n\n“The people who ordered it will come whether my roof is ready or not. Help me keep this flour dry, and I can still get the dough started.”\n\nSol, your repair kept the flour dry. The bread is ready for my customers, and I’ve brought this loaf for you. Thank you.\n\nReady for the oven. I’ll handle the hot tray. A little while ago I was moving flour sacks; now we have loaves to bake.\n\nI have Sol’s loaf. Walk with me along the path to his workshop. If you need to look at something, I’ll wait for you.\n\nPip can tell you what happened in the bakery. I’d better get back before my customers think I’ve eaten their bread.\n\nListen. Rain on the roof, but no drops in here. Before we start, I need to check the flour. Will you look with me?\n\nI can still see drops falling near the sacks. The opening needs to be covered before I can bring my flour back.\n\nYou have the spare tile. Sol is waiting beside the ladder. I’ll keep these sacks away from the puddle.",
  "textSha256": "d2dc87ded965bb33fbe5c1d9ee797ed99f3b759b9251ac82f7b8ca4ca6d25eef",
